//RS     stderr: String,
//RS }
//RS 
//RS /// Output goes to files, not pipes. A re-prompt loop would fill a pipe and stall
//RS /// against an unread reader, which reads as a hang for the wrong reason, and the
//RS /// size is taken before the text so a regression reports one number instead of
//RS /// replaying a 512MB prompt log.
